--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTED (parity with the web source)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pure presentational widget primitive — a parity port modeled on the documented ScoreBadge
shared surface. Reproduces every branch of the web source:
  * empty branch (web `entries.length === 0`) -> friendly TsEmptyState; message is the caller
    override or the localized `widget.detail.empty` default ("No details available"); optional
    glyph; the surface always renders (never a collapsed/blank box).
  * populated branch -> a vertically scrolling list of rows; each row = uppercase muted label
    (10px) on the left + value (14px primary, optional monospace) and an optional status chip on
    the right; a bottom hairline between rows (web `i < visible.length - 1`).
  * compact mode -> first four rows only (web `entries.slice(0, 4)`); the divider guard is
    recomputed against the sliced set.
  * value `?? '—'` fallback; badgeVariantMap (success->Success, warning->Warning, error->Danger,
    neutral->Neutral) mapped onto the native StatusKind.
Data        : none (pure presentational; parent widget owns fetching) -> no loading/error/stale/
              offline branches exist in the web source, so none are fabricated here.
Shared comps: @/components/ui -> TsBadge ; @/components/feedback -> TsEmptyState.
i18n        : every string resolves through ILocalizer (P1/S10); no hardcoded English in code
              (the empty-message default is a keyed fallback, mirroring ScoreBadge's score.aria).
a11y        : each (non-interactive) row carries a composed Narrator name "label: value[, badge]"
              built from the original (non-uppercased) label; TsEmptyState announces its message.
              No interactive elements exist in the web source, so none are added.
Telemetry   : WidgetDetailCardDiagnostics emits `view.opened slug=WidgetDetailCard` (P1/S11),
              PII-safe (never row labels/values).
UI-free logic lives in WidgetDetailCard.Model.cs (Registration/model/projection/diagnostics) so it
is Compile-linked into the headless test project; the WinUI view (WidgetDetailCard.cs) is exercised
by the app build.

